# MCP Server Briefing — Required at Conversation Start

At the start of every new conversation, read ALL MCP server tool and resource descriptors
from the mcps folder, then present the briefing below to the user before any other work.
Do not summarize or skip tools. Do not assume you already know the tool list — re-read it.

## Briefing Format

Present a single message at conversation open structured as:

```
## MCP Tools Active This Conversation — Mode: [Agent | Plan | Debug | Ask]

### REQUIRED in this mode
[list tools that must be called for the current mode]

### AVAILABLE in this mode (discretionary)
[list tools usable at agent judgment]

### NOT USED in this mode
[list tools that do not apply to this mode — state why]

### REQUIRES EXPLICIT USER INSTRUCTION BEFORE USE (any mode)
[list tools that must never be called without the user asking]

### REFERENCE RESOURCES AVAILABLE (any mode)
[list MCP resources — documents — and what they contain]
```

---

## Tool Mode Map

### Agent mode — full execution

**Required workflow (must call in this order for every Ansible change):**
- `validate-playbook` (ansible-mcp) — syntax check before touching a playbook
- `ansible_lint` (ansible) — lint after every edit
- `list_tasks` (sysoperator) — preview task execution before running
- `project-run-playbook` (ansible-mcp) — run the playbook
- `ansible-test-idempotence` (ansible-mcp) — confirm no changes on second run

**Required pre-task (before writing any task or role):**
- `inventory-graph` (ansible-mcp) — understand host/group structure
- `inventory-find-host` (ansible-mcp) — resolve merged variables for target host
- `ade_environment_info` (ansible) — confirm installed collections and Ansible version
- `zen_of_ansible` (ansible) — consult design philosophy when making structural decisions

**Discretionary (use when relevant):**
- `inventory-parse`, `inventory-diff` (ansible-mcp)
- `ansible-gather-facts` (ansible-mcp) — before writing tasks that depend on host state
- `ansible-capture-baseline` / `ansible-compare-states` (ansible-mcp) — for any change with drift risk
- `ansible-role` (ansible-mcp) — test a role in isolation
- `galaxy-install`, `galaxy-lock` (ansible-mcp)
- `vault-view`, `vault-encrypt`, `vault-decrypt` (ansible-mcp)
- `vault_encrypt_string`, `vault_decrypt_string` (sysoperator)
- `project-playbooks`, `list-projects` (ansible-mcp)
- `adt_check_env` (ansible)

**Not used in Agent mode unless task is explicitly about it:**
- `create_ansible_projects`, `define_and_build_execution_env` (ansible) — project scaffolding only
- `check_syntax` (sysoperator) — redundant with `validate-playbook`
- All AWS tools, `terraform` (sysoperator) — different domain
- All `cursor-ide-browser` tools — different domain

---

### Plan mode — read-only planning, no execution

**Required (must call before writing any plan involving Ansible):**
- `inventory-graph` (ansible-mcp) — understand what hosts/groups are in scope
- `inventory-find-host` (ansible-mcp) — resolve merged variables for any host referenced in plan
- `ade_environment_info` (ansible) — verify collections are installed before recommending modules
- `zen_of_ansible` (ansible) — consult before any structural or design recommendation
- `ansible-content-best-practices` resource (ansible) — fetch before answering any question about Ansible idiom, patterns, or best practice

**Discretionary:**
- `inventory-parse`, `inventory-diff` (ansible-mcp)
- `ansible-gather-facts` (ansible-mcp) — if live host state is relevant to the plan

**Not used in Plan mode:**
- `validate-playbook`, `ansible_lint`, `project-run-playbook`, `ansible-test-idempotence` — nothing is executed until plan is approved and mode switches to Agent
- `list_tasks` (sysoperator) — requires a runnable playbook; used post-edit in Agent mode
- All destructive or write tools

---

### Debug mode — evidence collection and diagnosis

**Required (per REQUIRED-EVIDENCE-NO-ASSUMPTIONS-ON-FAILURE rule):**
- `ansible-gather-facts` (ansible-mcp) — collect live host state before hypothesizing
- `ansible-fetch-logs` (ansible-mcp) — pull and analyze logs
- `ansible-diagnose-host` (ansible-mcp) — full health assessment
- `ansible-service-manager` (ansible-mcp) — verify service states

**Discretionary:**
- `ansible-log-hunter` (ansible-mcp) — correlate logs across sources
- `ansible-health-monitor` (ansible-mcp) — trend analysis
- `ansible-network-matrix` (ansible-mcp) — connectivity verification
- `ansible-capture-baseline` / `ansible-compare-states` (ansible-mcp)
- `ansible-remote-command` (ansible-mcp) — ad-hoc evidence only; prefer modules
- `ansible-performance-baseline` (ansible-mcp)
- `validate-playbook`, `ansible_lint` — if a task file is being edited as part of a fix
- `ansible-content-best-practices` resource — if fix involves idiomatic questions

**Not used in Debug mode:**
- `project-run-playbook`, `ansible-test-idempotence` — only after fix is confirmed and mode returns to Agent
- All AWS tools, `terraform`, browser tools

---

### Ask mode — conversational and informational only

**Required for any Ansible design or idiom question:**
- `zen_of_ansible` (ansible)
- `ansible-content-best-practices` resource (ansible)

**Discretionary:**
- `ade_environment_info` (ansible) — if question involves installed state
- `inventory-graph`, `inventory-find-host` (ansible-mcp) — if question involves host structure

**Not used in Ask mode:**
- All execution, lint, run, diagnostic, and write tools

---

## Tools Requiring Explicit User Instruction — Any Mode

Never call the following without the user explicitly requesting:

| Tool | Server | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `ansible-auto-heal` | ansible-mcp | Automatically modifies live systems |
| `vault-rekey` | ansible-mcp | Destructive — rotates vault password |
| `ade_setup_environment` | ansible | Modifies dev environment packages |
| `define_and_build_execution_env` | ansible | Builds and pushes EE images |
| `create_ansible_projects` | ansible | Scaffolds project structure on disk |
| `project-bootstrap`, `register-project` | ansible-mcp | Modifies project registry |
| `create-playbook`, `create-role-structure` | ansible-mcp | Creates files on disk |
| `terraform` | sysoperator | Infrastructure changes, separate domain |
| `aws_*` (all 10 tools) | sysoperator | AWS infrastructure changes |
| All `browser_*` tools | cursor-ide-browser | Browser automation, separate domain |

---

## Reference Resources (available in all modes)

Fetched via `FetchMcpResource` — read-only documents, never "run":

| Resource URI | Server | Content |
|---|---|---|
| `guidelines://ansible-content-best-practices` | ansible | Full Ansible coding guidelines and idiom reference |
| `guidelines://execution-environment-rules` | ansible | Rules for building execution environments |
| `guidelines://execution-environment-sample` | ansible | Sample EE definition |
| `guidelines://execution-environment-schema` | ansible | EE YAML schema |

---

## Tools Not Covered in ansible-mcp-first.mdc or Other Existing Rules

The following tools exist in your MCP servers but are NOT mentioned in any workspace `.mdc` rule.
They are available but have no rule-defined workflow:

**ansible server:**
- `zen_of_ansible` — should be used for design decisions (not in any rule)
- `ansible-content-best-practices` resource — should be used for idiom questions (not in any rule)
- `ade_setup_environment` — environment setup (explicit request only)
- `define_and_build_execution_env` — EE build (explicit request only)
- `create_ansible_projects` — project scaffolding (explicit request only)
- `adt_check_env`, `list_available_tools` — env diagnostics (discretionary)
- `execution-environment-*` resources — EE reference docs (discretionary)

**ansible-mcp server:**
- `inventory-diff` — compare inventory states (discretionary)
- `ansible-auto-heal` — automated healing (explicit request only)
- `ansible-performance-baseline` — performance baselining (discretionary)
- `project-bootstrap`, `register-project`, `list-projects` — project management (explicit request only)
- `create-playbook` — playbook scaffolding (explicit request only)
- `ansible-network-matrix` — connectivity matrix (discretionary in Debug)

**sysoperator server:**
- `terraform` and all `aws_*` tools — different domain entirely (explicit request only)
- `run_playbook` — use `project-run-playbook` from ansible-mcp instead; sysoperator version is a fallback

**cursor-ide-browser server:**
- All browser tools — web automation, separate domain entirely (explicit request only)
